# ::stuff tracks TeX Live's rolling tlnet archive, whose per-revision
# tarballs are DELETED upstream within days — by the time a synced ebuild
# reaches this image the distfile is a 404 on every CTAN mirror
# (texlive-luatex r79730, 2026-08-10: gone from tu-chemnitz and gust.org.pl
# alike, killed the whole post-kernel emerge; texlive-core 2026-r3 pinned
# texlive-scripts.r80004 and CTAN had already rotated it out, 2026-08-21).
#
# 2026-08-10 -> 2026-11-07: this file used to mask dev-texlive/*::stuff and
# >texlive-core-2026-r1::stuff outright. On 2026-10-06 the ::stuff snapshot
# below was deliberately unmasked, fetched the same day and installed on the
# host AND in every hard rootfs (gpkgs of that date in the shared pool) — but
# the blanket mask stayed, so the next 'update-seed' (--update @installed)
# DOWNGRADED the whole stack to ::gentoo (texlive-core 2026-r6 -> r2 built
# from source, 12 dev-texlive modules from stale pool gpkgs) and died on a
# file collision: ::gentoo's texlive-core-2026-r2 ships
# texmf-dist/dvips/xdvipsk/xdvipsk-cid.pro, and so does the pool's
# texlive-binextra-2026_p77772-r1-1 gpkg (::pwr copy, built 2026-08-06).
# Lesson: a mask that says "unmask deliberately when a bump is wanted" must be
# re-pinned to the new snapshot the day the bump is installed, or it becomes a
# downgrade order. Same shape as the libfmt/cudnn and opera holds in
# zz-image.mask (gentoo-live-image failures.md §34).
#
# Holds: everything ABOVE the installed 2026-10-06 snapshot stays masked
# (future tlnet revisions rot before pkgs runs); the snapshot itself is
# visible so --update @installed keeps it. To take a newer ::stuff bump:
# sync, fetch the same day on the host, install, then move every line below
# to the new version in the same commit (host copy: /etc/portage/package.mask/texlive-stuff).
>app-text/texlive-core-2026-r6::stuff
>dev-texlive/texlive-basic-2026_p72890-r3::stuff
>dev-texlive/texlive-bibtexextra-2026_p79975-r1::stuff
>dev-texlive/texlive-binextra-2026_p80064-r1::stuff
>dev-texlive/texlive-fontsextra-2026_p80219::stuff
>dev-texlive/texlive-fontsrecommended-2026_p54074-r1::stuff
>dev-texlive/texlive-fontutils-2026_p61207-r2::stuff
>dev-texlive/texlive-formatsextra-2026_p72250-r4::stuff
>dev-texlive/texlive-latex-2026_p80015::stuff
>dev-texlive/texlive-latexextra-2026_p80217::stuff
>dev-texlive/texlive-latexrecommended-2026_p78568-r4::stuff
>dev-texlive/texlive-luatex-2026_p79926-r1::stuff
>dev-texlive/texlive-pictures-2026_p80119::stuff
>dev-texlive/texlive-plaingeneric-2026_p79318-r2::stuff
>dev-texlive/texlive-xetex-2026_p78834-r5::stuff

# 2026-11-07, ryzenhard (and every image whose TeX stack is the ::pwr copy:
# amdkdehard, corehard, intelhard): ::gentoo bumped texlive-core to 2026-r2,
# which builds xdvipsk and ships texmf-dist/dvips/xdvipsk/xdvipsk-cid.pro;
# ::gentoo's texlive-binextra-2026_p77772-r1 deletes that file in src_install.
# The ::pwr binextra is the SAME version without the rm (its core, r1, has
# --disable-xdvipsk), so portage keeps the installed ::pwr module and moves
# only the core to ::gentoo -> file collision, texlive-core NOT merged.
# Hold ::gentoo's core away from a ::pwr-module stack; the ::pwr r1 is then
# rebuilt against kpathsea 6.4.2 (>=6.4.0:=). Drop this line when the ::pwr
# dev-texlive copies are bumped to a snapshot whose binextra matches a
# ::gentoo core, or when the image takes its stack from ::stuff (nvidiahard).
>=app-text/texlive-core-2026-r2::gentoo
